# Keep the build context small and keep secrets and client data out of it.
# Anything listed here is invisible to every COPY in the Dockerfile.

# Rebuilt inside the image by the deps stage.
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.*

# Rebuilt inside the image by `pnpm build`.
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# REAL CLIENT DOCUMENTS. These are gitignored for the same reason; the rule is
# repeated here because a docker build reads the working tree, not the index,
# so an uncommitted PDF would otherwise be baked into a pushed image layer.
documents
test-docs

# Regenerated inside the image by `pnpm vendor:ocr` at prebuild. Excluding it
# also stops a stale local copy from shadowing the vendored one.
public/tesseract

# Secrets. .env.local holds the real Gemini key; on Cloud Run every secret is
# mounted from Secret Manager instead, so none of these belong in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Leftover Ollama weights from before inference moved to the Gemini API.
models

# Local tooling and history that would only bust the layer cache.
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.playwright-mcp
*.log
.DS_Store

# Docs and specs. Nothing in the running image reads them.
docs
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
